  "id": "autonomic-ganglia",
  "term": "autonomic ganglia",
  "definition": "Autonomic ganglia are clusters of nerve cells within the autonomic nervous system where signals from preganglionic fibers coming from the central nervous system are passed to neurons whose fibers go on to target organs. They also include supporting cells, intrinsic neurons, and some preganglionic fibers traveling through to other ganglia.",
